  are unrelated. No tests, no test runner in [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m.

  [1mThe fork, in one sentence:[0m [38;5;153mlogin[39m already receives [38;5;153musername[39m — the identity of the person logging in — and the only call
  site has nothing else available, so "add a [38;5;153muserId[39m parameter" only makes sense if [38;5;153muserId[39m is something [3mother[0m than the
  username, and where it comes from determines whether this is a one-line signature change or new structure.

  - [1m[38;5;153muserId[39m is a caller-supplied correlation/session ID[0m (e.g. a device or request ID generated before submit) — cheap,
    one new param plus a generator at the call site, no new module. Locks in the convention that callers own ID
    generation.
  - [1m[38;5;153muserId[39m is the account's stable internal ID[0m — the call site can't supply it; pre-authentication the browser only
    knows the typed username. Would need the ID to come back [3mfrom[0m the login response instead, which means the parameter
    you asked for isn't the right shape. Cheap to change now, expensive after other callers depend on it.
  - [1m"Track" means a real logging/analytics sink[0m, not [38;5;153mconsole.log[39m — that's a new subsystem, and I'd re-classify as
    architectural and write a spec first.

  [1mMy recommendation:[0m the first option, if what you want is to correlate login attempts. It's the only one where "add a
  [38;5;153muserId[39m parameter" is literally the right change, and it stays a handful of lines in one file.
